Workflow hardening: `permissions: contents: read` at top level, widened only in the deploy job; `persist-credentials: false`; Node 16 → 20; `--ignore-scripts`; `concurrency` with `cancel-in-progress`; no outbound calls anywhere.

## Push commands (dummy URL)

`git init` must run in `my_website/`, **not** the repo root — GitHub only reads workflows from the root, and there's no `.git` yet:

```bash
cd my_website
ls info.md .github/workflows/deploy.yml   # confirm you're in the right directory

git init -b main
git add .
git status --short          # review: public/ must NOT appear
git commit -m "Personal research profile site"

git remote add origin https://github.com/example-user/lydia-moreno-site.git
git remote -v               # verify before pushing
git push -u origin main
```

Run the workflow with the GitHub CLI:

```bash
gh workflow list                          # find "Deploy Site"
gh workflow run "Deploy Site" --ref main  # workflow_dispatch trigger
gh run list --workflow "Deploy Site"
gh run watch
```

Then set **Settings → Pages → Source: Deploy from a branch → `gh-pages` / (root)**.

